{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/434196-how-do-you-pronounce-qin","id":434196,"title":"How do YOU pronounce Qin?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-09T10:43:25-07:00","id":434196,"title":"How do YOU pronounce Qin?","content":"I never did figure out how to pronounce the name of the alien race of &quot;slugs&quot; in biosuits. I did read in the core Trinity book that humanity used the word for an old form of opera from Beijing, Qin, but my Mandarin, or Cantonese for that matter, is severely lacking to know how to pronounce that word. Any Chinese speakers out there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T10:59:37-07:00","id":434206,"title":"","content":"Not a Mandarin or Cantonese speaker, but I've always used something close to &quot;Chen / Chin&quot; (possibly incorrectly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:29:21-07:00","id":434270,"title":"","content":"A very h-tinged ch sound, followed by the ean in lean. <a href=\"https://translate.google.com/#zh-CN/en/%E7%A7%A6\" target=\"_blank\">Give Google Translate's Listen function a whirl.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:52:06-07:00","id":434484,"title":"","content":"It's sort of halfway between &quot;keen&quot; and &quot;cheen.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T16:47:32-07:00","id":434853,"title":"","content":"I forgot about the audio feature on Google translate. That helped. To untrained ears it is really hard to get the pronunciation just right, but I think I got it.<br /> <br /> Thanks everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T22:27:03-07:00","id":435283,"title":"","content":"I suppose i should out myself as one of those ignorant enough of sino-tibetan language to assume the pronounciation was 'kwinn', by the time i realized my mistake the group were used to that sound and i felt it would be confusing to retcon the error. If it's of any defense, i was young and stupid at the time. The chinese pronounciation is clearly the intended sound, given the setting information concerning the name's origin.<br /> Added embarrasment for my choice of avatar...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Avatar related irony recognized. 03-10-2015, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:56:33-07:00","id":435703,"title":"","content":"It was the same for me Nihilist. It doesn't sound right to me unless I pronounce it <i>kwin</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:57:23-07:00","id":435704,"title":"","content":"Oh, the same goes for my avatar too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:37:24-07:00","id":435832,"title":"","content":"Also.... it's 2nd tone. So say it with a rising voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T22:32:52-07:00","id":436741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/434196-how-do-you-pronounce-qin?p=435283#post435283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose i should out myself as one of those ignorant enough of sino-tibetan language to assume the pronounciation was 'kwinn', by the time i realized my mistake the group were used to that sound and i felt it would be confusing to retcon the error. If it's of any defense, i was young and stupid at the time. The chinese pronounciation is clearly the intended sound, given the setting information concerning the name's origin.<br /> Added embarrasment for my choice of avatar...</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the books say there are characters in-setting that miss the proper pronunciation and say &quot;kwinn&quot; as well. Enough that it's considered an alternate nickname. If that helps you feel better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T00:01:01-07:00","id":436784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/434196-how-do-you-pronounce-qin?p=436741#post436741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, the books say there are characters in-setting that miss the proper pronunciation and say &quot;kwinn&quot; as well. Enough that it's considered an alternate nickname. If that helps you feel better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Much better! Where does it say that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T02:36:24-07:00","id":436860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/434196-how-do-you-pronounce-qin?p=435832#post435832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also.... it's 2nd tone. So say it with a rising voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice detail. This thread is making me want to make the conversion to proper pronounciation...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/434196-how-do-you-pronounce-qin?p=436741#post436741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, the books say there are characters in-setting that miss the proper pronunciation and say &quot;kwinn&quot; as well. Enough that it's considered an alternate nickname. If that helps you feel better.</div> </div> </div> </div>If any word could qualify for repurposing, it would be the one given to a sapient alien species to serve as a name. I don't really buy that, even if it was in an official source - who still read their news in the holographic, agent driven world of 2107? The sound would have been accessible to everyone from the beginning. So, if there is a move to call them something else it would be deliberate as opposed to a mispronounciation of a word they mostly hear and not read. If that makes sense...<br /> I thought the mispronounciation would be more common actually, you guys know your Chinese pronounciation. Respect.<br /> <br /> But, i'd love to know where that comes from too, my Alien Encounter books are still packed away - which is where i'd look first. What's the bet it comes from a Legionaire? Extra points if they are Australian to boot, because my Australian group chose by consesus to keep using 'kwin' after i learned the truth. The philistines. -smiles-<br /> <br /> Two slug avatars defending the wrong pronounciation of a slug-aliens name is giving me a persistent little grin. I have a wierd sense of humour...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T08:49:55-07:00","id":437082,"title":"","content":"People who speak languages that don't contain the appropriate sound for the &quot;q&quot; and don't have tones, or even the tones of Mandarin, are going to pronounce it differently. Whichever version of the pronunciation gets to be the dominant meme in a particular context is going to determine how people pronounce it. If the group is Chinese or from an area under the influence of the Middle Kingdom to the point that Mandarin is a language of acommodation, they are going to pronounce it as per above. Otherwise, they are going to covert it over to their phonetic system. So, probably to most speakers of Indo-European languages, &quot;cheen&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:26:01-07:00","id":437443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/434196-how-do-you-pronounce-qin?p=437082#post437082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who speak languages that don't contain the appropriate sound for the &quot;q&quot; and don't have tones, or even the tones of Mandarin, are going to pronounce it differently. Whichever version of the pronunciation gets to be the dominant meme in a particular context is going to determine how people pronounce it. If the group is Chinese or from an area under the influence of the Middle Kingdom to the point that Mandarin is a language of acommodation, they are going to pronounce it as per above. Otherwise, they are going to covert it over to their phonetic system. So, probably to most speakers of Indo-European languages, &quot;cheen&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great post, you seem to have a pretty solid grasp of this, i'm going to have to read up on tones.<br /> There is precedence for a word to be borrowed directly and in the case of aliens called the 'Qin', the word (when written) could actually show up in Chinese characters - perhaps even developing a glyph of its own over time. Because it seems to me that first contact is probably the single best reason to come up with an entirely new noun - even if that noun is based on a pre-existing word. But, i'm probably overthinking it.<br /> Thanks for the insight, Ajax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T18:33:57-07:00","id":437834,"title":"","content":"A couple of anthropology degrees and 3 years of Chinese can do that to you....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:29:32-07:00","id":463879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/434196-how-do-you-pronounce-qin?p=434484#post434484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's sort of halfway between &quot;keen&quot; and &quot;cheen.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ka-Ching!<br /> <br /> ...Sorry. I couldn't resist. Again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/434196-how-do-you-pronounce-qin?p=434270#post434270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A very h-tinged ch sound, followed by the ean in lean. <a href=\"https://translate.google.com/#zh-CN/en/%E7%A7%A6\" target=\"_blank\">Give Google Translate's Listen function a whirl.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This was useful, thank you. Before this thread, my mind always pronounced Qin as &quot;kin.&quot; And, genre-hopping aside, seeing Danerys on Game of Thrones pronounce the city of Quarth as &quot;kwarth&quot; and get corrected (it's actually pronounced &quot;karth&quot;) didn't help matters. Then again, there's no China in Westeros or Essos (or even Soth